# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRETTIER DOES NOT FORMAT MARKDOWN HERE.
#
# Not a preference — its markdown printer is NOT IDEMPOTENT, and a formatter
# that is not idempotent is broken by definition: `format(format(x))` must
# equal `format(x)`.
#
# Measured on this repo (2026-09-06): a list item followed by a blank line and
# an indented paragraph gains FOUR MORE SPACES of indentation on every
# `--write`, without converging. TODO.md had reached column 44 and its content
# was already mangled — a nested list flattened into prose, a sentence dedented
# mid-way — because `bun run format` had been quietly deepening it for months.
#
# Not configurable away: proseWrap preserve / never / always all oscillate.
# Not fixed upstream: prettier 3.9.6 does it too, and faster than 2.8.8.
# Minimal repro is four lines (see UPSTREAM.md).
#
# And nothing is lost. Every one of the 110 non-markdown files in the repo is
# idempotent, so the gate keeps its value where the value is; markdown here is
# hand-written prose that a doc site renders, with no consistency problem for a
# formatter to solve. Do not re-enable this without checking idempotency first.
*.md
